-- Shape:
--   ns.REP_REWARDS["<faction name>"] = { factionId = <id>,
--     rewards = { { standing = "<standing>", item = <itemId>, name = "<name>" }, ... } }
--   ns.GEMS[itemId] = { color = "<Red|Yellow|Blue|Orange|Green|Purple>", cut = "<name>" }
--   ns.META_GEMS[itemId] = { cut = "<name>" }
--   ns.ENCHANT_ITEMS["<slot>"] = { { id = <itemId>, name = "<name>" }, ... }
--   ns.LEG_ARMOR[n] = { id = <itemId>, name = "<name>", profession = "<profession>" }
--   ns.WEAPON_SCOPES[n] = { id = <itemId>, name = "<name>" }
--
-- Item ids are the load-bearing data; the addon resolves id -> name/icon/stats
-- through the game client at runtime. Name fields are carried only to make this
-- file readable and its diffs reviewable by a human.
--
-- Coverage notes from this generation pass:
--   * ns.GEMS and ns.META_GEMS are Burning Crusade only: vanilla AtlasLoot data has
--     no Jewelcrafting module at all (the profession did not exist pre-TBC), so
--     there is no classic cut-gem source to read. This is a genuine source gap, not
--     an extraction failure.
--   * ns.LEG_ARMOR mixes two source professions: Leatherworking's own "Leg Armor"
--     items (Burning Crusade only; vanilla Leatherworking never added leg-specific
--     armor, only generic Armor Kits usable on any leather piece, which are not
--     included here) and Tailoring's Spellthread items (Burning Crusade only), the
--     cloth-wearer equivalent of leg armor. Both carry a profession field so the
--     addon can tell them apart.
--   * ns.WEAPON_SCOPES covers Engineering-only gun/bow scopes from both eras.
--   * ns.ENCHANT_ITEMS covers only permanent slot enchants recoverable from a
--     labeled "<Slot> - Enhancements" source category (Weapon, 2H Weapon, Cloak,
--     Chest, Feet, Hand, Shield, Wrist, Ring). Temporary weapon oils, wands, rods
--     and enchanting reagents (the source's own "Oil"/"Wands"/"Misc" categories)
--     are deliberately excluded as not permanent gear enchants. No Shoulder-slot
--     enchant category exists in this AtlasLoot data for classic or TBC (shoulder
--     enchants in this era come from reputation, not a craftable recipe), so
--     ns.ENCHANT_ITEMS has no ["Shoulder"] key; a shoulder enchant's source is a
--     faction instead and shows up in ns.REP_REWARDS.
--   * ns.REP_REWARDS lists every reward row AtlasLoot has for a faction (gear,
--     recipes, tokens alike), not just equippable items, because the task calling
--     for this file asked for "every reward," not just gear.

